            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0183" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3652: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-27T18:00:00+08:00">January 27, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 27—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A Japanese member of the Municipal Council who usually acts as liaison officer
                    between the Japanese Naval Attaché and the Council has requested that a state of
                    emergency declaration should be issued today. <pb facs="0184" n="80"
                        xml:id="pg80"/> The Secretary General promised to call a meeting of the
                    Municipal Council for the consideration of the request today.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
